      ],
      "text": "the page shell    = the outer wrapper: what kind of document this is, what the browser tab says, how it fits a small screen    (head)\nthe look          = the colors for day and night, the two panes, the even letters of the flow text, and the marks that say a line can be clicked    (style)\nthe frame         = the empty shapes the page starts with: a narrow side column and a wide reading column, no words in them yet    (main)\n\nimports           = FileTree, the ready-made list of file names for the side column, from trees.js next to this page\n\nesc               = text made safe to show: the sharp letters of a file appear as letters, not as page instructions    (esc)\nprojs             = every project with its files, each file held as two things:\n    the map           = the explanations written for that file, each one tied to the file lines it talks about\n    the real text     = the file itself, line by line\ncur               = the project and the file on the screen now\nbyId              = an explanation found by its number\nblockId           = the first explanation that covers a named block, so a name in parentheses can become something to click\nchildrenOf        = under each explanation and each of its steps, the closer looks that hang there\n    a closer look     = an explanation of one single line of a bigger explanation, folded away until the person opens it\nopenSet           = the closer looks the person has opened\ncovered           = for every explanation that says the same flow in more detail, the shorter explanation that stands over it\ntops              = the explanations that hang under nothing and stand under no shorter explanation, always shown\nlines             = the real text of the open file, kept only to count the lines that carry something\nft                = the file-name list in the side column\nrows              = the box in the reading column where everything the person reads is placed\nmsg               = one sentence in the middle of the page when there is nothing to show    (msg)\n\nthe first load    = the page asks for the list of projects, then for each file its map and its real text\n    the list says, for example: the project decompiler with the files dmap.py, SKILL.md, web.html\n    a file with no map     = opens as an empty map, so the person still sees the file\n    a file with no text    = drops out of the list\n    nothing arrives        = the sentence asks the person to serve the folder and run dmap map\n    everything arrives     = the side list is built, and the first file of the first project opens\n\nthe project bar   = a click opens the list of project names, a second click closes it\nthe project pick  = a click on a name puts that project in the side list and opens its first file\nopen              = one file placed on the screen: its explanations sorted for finding, its closer looks grouped under the line each one hangs on, nothing open yet    (open)\n\nstartOf           = the first file line an explanation covers, so the explanations can be shown in file order    (startOf)\nendOf             = the last file line an explanation covers    (endOf)\nfmtSpans          = the covered lines written short, like 7-59    (fmtSpans)\nnonBlank          = how many lines between two numbers carry something, for the hidden-lines mark    (nonBlank)\nfirstToken        = the first word of a text line, lowercased, with a leading ! dropped    (firstToken)\nchunksOf          = an explanation text cut into chunks, one chunk per step, each chunk tied to the step it belongs to    (chunksOf)\ncallLinks         = every name in parentheses that this file also explains, turned into something the person can click    (callLinks)\nkidsOf            = for one explanation, the lines that have a closer look hanging on them    (kidsOf)\nchunkHtml         = one chunk turned into what the person sees: its lines, its links, and any closer look opened in place    (chunkHtml)\n    flush             = the lines waited for so far, laid down as one block, so an opened closer look can stand between them    (flush)\nentryHtml         = every chunk of one explanation, in order    (entryHtml)\nexpansionHtml     = an opened closer look, with its own heading over it and a way to close it again    (expansionHtml)\nopenPath          = every step from a chosen explanation up to the top opened, so a click reaches an explanation that lies buried    (openPath)\ndeepest           = for one explanation, the one that says the same flow in more detail that the person opened, followed down step by step to the last one opened    (deepest)\nrender            = the reading column drawn again: the explanations in file order, a mark for every stretch of lines no explanation covers, and the count in the strip on top    (render)\ncloseTree         = one closer look closed, and every closer look under it    (closeTree)\n\nthe click answer  = one place answers every click in the reading column:\n    a name in parentheses  = its explanation opens and the page slides to it\n    a line with one name   = a click anywhere on the line opens that name\n    a line with a look     = the closer look opens, or closes when it was already open\n    the heading of a look  = that look closes",
